1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,420
Chai Corner began as one stall,
with Ravi doing it all alone.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,346
Now it has five outlets.

3
00:00:06,346 --> 00:00:08,307
But is it actually doing well?

4
00:00:08,857 --> 00:00:10,660
Kabir says, sales are up.

5
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:11,876
We're doing great.

6
00:00:12,176 --> 00:00:14,251
Asha asks, are the staff happy?

7
00:00:14,251 --> 00:00:16,226
Meena asks, are the customers?

8
00:00:16,526 --> 00:00:18,561
Everyone has a different answer.

9
00:00:18,561 --> 00:00:19,782
So who is right?

10
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:22,711
Bigger is not the same as better.

11
00:00:22,711 --> 00:00:24,764
Ravi must measure effectiveness.

12
00:00:25,464 --> 00:00:28,281
So, what is organizational effectiveness?

13
00:00:28,581 --> 00:00:33,284
Organizational effectiveness means
how well an organization achieves its

14
00:00:33,284 --> 00:00:34,184
goals.

15
00:00:34,569 --> 00:00:38,060
Think of it as a report card
for the whole organization.

16
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:40,175
Remember episode one?

17
00:00:40,175 --> 00:00:42,711
Effective means doing the right things.

18
00:00:43,061 --> 00:00:45,913
Efficient means doing
things right, with no waste.

19
00:00:46,263 --> 00:00:47,225
You need both.

20
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:49,854
But doing the wrong thing
well is still wrong.

21
00:00:50,504 --> 00:00:53,058
There are four ways to
judge effectiveness.

22
00:00:53,508 --> 00:00:54,408
One.

23
00:00:53,988 --> 00:00:55,814
The goal attainment approach.

24
00:00:55,814 --> 00:00:57,415
Did we reach our goals?

25
00:00:57,415 --> 00:01:00,220
Ravi aimed for five
outlets, and got there.

26
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:01,470
Two.

27
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:02,875
The system resource approach.

28
00:01:02,875 --> 00:01:07,655
Can we get scarce things from outside,
like milk, money, and skilled staff?

29
00:01:08,005 --> 00:01:08,905
Three.

30
00:01:08,641 --> 00:01:10,716
The internal process approach.

31
00:01:10,716 --> 00:01:14,293
Does work inside run smoothly,
with little conflict?

32
00:01:14,643 --> 00:01:15,543
And four.

33
00:01:15,446 --> 00:01:17,092
The stakeholder approach.

34
00:01:17,092 --> 00:01:21,950
Is every group the firm affects happy:
customers, staff, owners, suppliers,

35
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:22,900
and society?

36
00:01:23,550 --> 00:01:25,978
Managers keep score with six signs.

37
00:01:26,328 --> 00:01:31,191
Profit, productivity, customer
satisfaction, employee satisfaction, growth,

38
00:01:31,191 --> 00:01:34,827
and adaptability, which means
changing with the times.

39
00:01:35,477 --> 00:01:37,689
Now look back at Ravi's whole journey.

40
00:01:38,039 --> 00:01:42,100
He started alone, with a hundred
customers, and people walking away.

41
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:46,214
He built a team, and learned
to plan, organize, and control.

42
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:50,370
He opened a second outlet at the
bus stand, then grew to five.

43
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:54,306
And he learned to decide, delegate,
and choose the right span.

44
00:01:54,956 --> 00:01:56,593
So, the scorecard.

45
00:01:56,593 --> 00:01:57,818
Goals reached.

46
00:01:57,818 --> 00:01:59,272
Resources secured.

47
00:01:59,272 --> 00:02:00,496
Smooth inside.

48
00:02:00,496 --> 00:02:02,007
Stakeholders happy.

49
00:02:02,357 --> 00:02:04,514
Chai Corner is not just bigger.

50
00:02:04,514 --> 00:02:05,742
It is effective.

51
00:02:07,142 --> 00:02:08,081
Quick check.

52
00:02:08,081 --> 00:02:12,000
Ravi asks customers, staff, and
suppliers if they are happy.

53
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,587
Which approach is this?

54
00:02:15,487 --> 00:02:17,019
The stakeholder approach!

55
00:02:17,019 --> 00:02:20,391
He checks that every group
the business affects is happy.

56
00:02:20,991 --> 00:02:22,000
So, remember.

57
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:27,489
Organizational effectiveness is how
well an organization achieves its goals.

58
00:02:27,839 --> 00:02:32,968
Judge it four ways: goals, resources,
internal process, and stakeholders.

59
00:02:33,318 --> 00:02:35,896
And effective means
doing the right things.

60
00:02:35,896 --> 00:02:37,907
Efficient means doing them right.

61
00:02:38,507 --> 00:02:39,979
That's the full series.

62
00:02:39,979 --> 00:02:44,450
From one stall to five outlets, you
now know the principles of management.
